  "revision_changes_vs_v4": "V1 (2ac3ad0) rejected by the owner: too many borders. V2 (73a2823) merged the sky, both lattice doors and the moon/cloud layer into one back plate, shrank the clear rim 2.5 -> 1.0 mm and rendered clear acrylic see-through in the assembly preview. V3 (657a484) recomposed the scene but the owner prefers V2 (\"v2가 낫다고 한거야\"). V4 (a2a83cd) = V2 plus two owner requests: the blossom tree printed diagonally into the back panel and Len \"seated\" by cropping her raster at the seat line. V5 = the owner's V4 feedback (\"거슬림, 그리고 벛곷나무도 별도 에셋으로 빼, + 나무는 대각선 배치하라고\"): (a) the cropped legs bother him, so the whole 84 mm figure is shown again (no crop) and she is seated ON the serpent: the serpent is enlarged 55 -> 70 mm and moved to x=150 so its lower coil rises to her seat line behind her hips, her hanging legs and boots are in front of the coil and her feet reach the base (the bud-guard riser between the legs is the only clear support); (b) the blossom tree is its own cut plate again (5 pieces, 6 slots, 11 closed paths), rotated 25 deg clockwise (86 mm unrotated art height -> 104.3 x 94.2 mm alpha box, larger than V4's printed 80 mm) and placed diagonally across the moon behind the serpent and Len with its tab under the trunk; its canopy contour is a 2.5 mm vector closing of the ink silhouette (clear acrylic between the blossoms, +836 mm2 = 22% of the ink area) so it passes the laser_paths segment gate at the standard 1.0 mm rim (725 of 895 segments). Every rim is 1.0 mm; nothing of Len is cropped.",
  "preview_rendering": "clear acrylic see-through on a dark mauve ground: plate bodies unfilled, one 0.26 mm lit-edge stroke per plate, tabs clipped at the shoulder (inside the slots); base slab shows its front side band",
